on estimates: Summary for England and Wales, mid-2023</t></si><si><t>MYE2: Males by single year of age and sex for local authorities in England and Wales, mid-2023</t></si><si><t>MYE2: Females by single year of age and sex for local authorities in England and Wales, mid-2023</t></si><si><t>MYE2: Persons by single year of age and sex for local authorities in England and Wales, mid-2023</t></si><si><t>MYE3: Components of population change for local authorities in England and Wales, mid-2023</t></si><si><t>Estimated Population mid-2023</t></si><si><t>Mid-2023</t></si><si><t>MYE4: Population estimates: Summary for England and Wales, mid-2011 to mid-2023</t></si><si><t>2023 people per sq. km</t></si><si><t>2022 people per sq. km2</t></si><si><t>MYE5: Population density for local authorities in England and Wales, mid-2011 to mid-2023</t></si><si><t>MYE6: Median age of population for local authorities in England and Wales, mid-2011 to mid-2023</t></si><si><r><t xml:space="preserve">The data tables in this spreadsheet were originally published at </t></r><r><rPr><sz val="12"/><rFont val="Arial"/><family val="2"/></rPr><t>9.30am 15 July 2024.</t></r></si><si><t>Date published: 15 July 2024</t></si><si><t>Release number: MYE23</t></si><si><r><t xml:space="preserve">Internal migration for counties, regions, England and Wales: </t></r><r><rPr><sz val="12"/><rFont val="Arial"/><family val="2"/></rPr><t>we are only able to provide internal migration netflows for counties, regions and England and Wales for mid-2023; inflows and outflows are unavailable. This reflects a different supply of internal migration estimates for mid-2023 which is not as detailed our regular method. Further details can be found in our methodology guide.</t></r><r><rPr><b/><sz val="12"/><rFont val="Arial"/><family val="2"/></rPr><t xml:space="preserve"> </t></r></si><si><r><rPr><b/><sz val="12"/><color theme="1"/><rFont val="Arial"/><family val="2"/></rPr><t>Geographical coverage:</t></r><r><rPr><sz val="12"/><color theme="1"/><rFont val="Arial"/><family val="2"/></rPr><t xml:space="preserve"> these statistics cover England and Wales only. Estimates for the whole of the UK, covering mid-2023, will be published later in the year.</t></r></si><si><t xml:space="preserve">Further information about population estimates can be found on the Office for National Statistics (ONS) website and elsewhere via the links included below: </t></si><si><t>The next publication is scheduled for summer 2025.</t></si><si><r><rPr><b/><sz val="12"/><rFont val="Arial"/><family val="2"/></rPr><t>Rounding:</t></r><r><rPr><sz val="12"/><rFont val="Arial"/><family val="2"/></rPr><t xml:space="preserve"> estimates are presented unrounded. Unrounded estimates are published to enable and encourage further calculations and analysis. However, the estimates should not be taken to be accurate to the level of detail provided. More information on the accuracy of the estimates is available in the Quality and Methodology document (QMI).</t></r></si><si><r><rPr><b/><sz val="12"/><rFont val="Arial"/><family val="2"/></rPr><t>Use of 2023 Local authorities:</t></r><r><rPr><sz val="12"/><rFont val="Arial"/><family val="2"/></rPr><t xml:space="preserve"> this spreadsheet uses boundaries for England and Wales that existed at publication, which includes the changes made in April 2023.</t></r></si><si><r><rPr><b/><sz val="12"/><rFont val="Arial"/><family val="2"/></rPr><t>Revision to mid-2022 population estimates</t></r><r><rPr><sz val="12"/><rFont val="Arial"/><family val="2"/></rPr><t>: Population estimates for mid-2022 have been revised to account for improvements to the disaggregation of international migration from the UK level down to local authority by age and sex.</t></r></si></sst>